  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Same-Origin Policy: Origins, Sites & Who Enforces",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Origin Is A Triple",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Origin = scheme + host + port. All three must match, exactly, byte for byte."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Compared to `https://a.com`",
            "Same?",
            "Differs by"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`http://a.com`",
              "no",
              "scheme"
            ],
            [
              "`https://api.a.com`",
              "no",
              "host"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com:8443`",
              "no",
              "port"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com/y`",
              "yes",
              "path only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Path is NOT part of an origin",
            "`/x` and `/y` are same-origin, always",
            "`document.domain` relaxation: removed, dead",
            "Never design a new system around it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Site Is Not Origin"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Same-site",
                "lines": [
                  "eTLD+1 + scheme",
                  "`a.example.com`",
                  "`b.example.com`",
                  "cookie scope"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Same-origin",
                "lines": [
                  "scheme+host+port",
                  "strictly equal",
                  "SOP scope",
                  "stricter"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Enforces It"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "SOP is a browser rule, not a server rule",
            "`curl`, Postman, server-to-server: unaffected",
            "Browser extensions bypass CORS entirely",
            "So CORS never replaces server-side authz"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Read Blocked, Send Allowed",
          "text": "SOP blocks reading the cross-origin response; it often does not block sending the request. That asymmetry is the root of CSRF."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The `null` Origin",
          "items": [
            "From sandboxed iframes",
            "From `file://` pages",
            "From some redirect chains",
            "Never treat `null` as trusted"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// preflighted: JSON content-type",
            "fetch(u, {method:'POST',",
            "  headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},",
            "  body:'{}'})  // OPTIONS fires first"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "What CORS Opens: Reads, Not Sends",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backward Compatibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`<img>`, `<script>`, `<link rel=stylesheet>` load cross-origin",
            "`<iframe>` embeds, `<form>` posts cross-origin",
            "All free since 1996 — CORS could not break them",
            "So CORS only gates `fetch`/XHR reads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What CORS Actually Is"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cross-Origin Resource Sharing: a server opt-in",
            "Server says 'this origin may read my response'",
            "Not authentication, not authorization",
            "Browser is the enforcer — server already ran it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Mental Model",
          "text": "CORS is a read-permission handshake between browser and server, negotiated purely with HTTP headers."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Send vs Read"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cross-origin action",
            "Allowed?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`<img>` / `<script>` load",
              "yes, embed"
            ],
            [
              "`<form>` POST send",
              "yes, **sent**"
            ],
            [
              "`fetch` request send",
              "often sent"
            ],
            [
              "read `fetch` response",
              "==blocked== unless CORS"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "JS on `app.com`",
              "fetch `api.com`",
              "server runs it",
              "browser checks ACAO",
              "JS reads or blocked"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Curl Ignores All Of It"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "curl https://api.a.com/me \\",
            "  -H 'Origin: https://evil.com'",
            "# server answers; no CORS gate"
          ],
          "note": "only browsers enforce CORS"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Using CORS to block scripts or curl",
            "Treating CORS as a login check",
            "Allowlisting the `null` origin",
            "Leaning on `document.domain` to merge subdomains"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Is `https://a.com` same-origin with `https://a.com:443`?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "**Yes** — 443 is the default https port",
            "Default ports are normalized away",
            "But `:8443` is a different origin"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Where CORS Fits",
          "text": "SOP is the wall; CORS is the door the ==server== opens for named origins, for reads only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anatomy of a CORS Exchange: Origin & ACAO",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `Origin` Header",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser adds `Origin` automatically on cross-origin fetch/XHR",
            "JS cannot set it, spoof it, or delete it",
            "Sent on simple requests too — server always knows",
            "So the server can decide before it answers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "JS `fetch`",
              "browser adds `Origin`",
              "server",
              "ACAO check",
              "JS reads or throws"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "ACAO value",
            "Valid?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`*`",
              "yes, no credentials"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com`",
              "yes, exact echo"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com, https://b.com`",
              "no, lists banned"
            ],
            [
              "`https://*.a.com`",
              "no, no inner wildcard"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const o = req.headers.origin",
            "if (ALLOW.has(o)) {",
            "  res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', o)",
            "  res.set('Vary', 'Origin')  // cache safety",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Request Flavors"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "cross-origin fetch",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0",
                "c1_1"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "cross-origin fetch",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "simple",
                "shape": "box"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "preflighted",
                "shape": "box"
              },
