              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Failure Looks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Request executes; response reaches the browser",
            "Browser discards it before JS sees it",
            "JS gets `TypeError: Failed to fetch`",
            "No status, no headers — deliberately opaque"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "'But I Can See It!'",
          "text": "DevTools shows the response body even when JS is blocked. The network tab is not JS. Opacity prevents error detail becoming a side channel."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Safelisted Response Headers",
          "items": [
            "`Cache-Control`, `Content-Language`",
            "`Content-Length`, `Content-Type`",
            "`Expires`, `Last-Modified`",
            "`Pragma` — that is the whole list"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Exposed Headers & Simple-Request Rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Response Headers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Without opt-in, JS sees only safelisted response headers",
            "`Access-Control-Expose-Headers` widens that set",
            "Common bite: `X-Request-Id` invisible until listed",
            "Same for an echoed `Authorization`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Errors Need Headers Too",
          "text": "CORS headers must appear on 4xx/5xx responses. Otherwise the client sees a CORS error instead of your real 500."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "All Conditions, Not Any",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A request is simple only if method, headers, content-type and body shape ALL qualify. One violation forces a preflight."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Dimension",
            "Simple if"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "method",
              "`GET`, `HEAD`, `POST`"
            ],
            [
              "content-type",
              "form-urlencoded, multipart, text/plain"
            ],
            [
              "headers",
              "safelisted only"
            ],
            [
              "body",
              "no `ReadableStream`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` always preflight",
            "`application/json` is the #1 accidental preflight",
            "Any custom header forces the probe",
            "No listener on `XMLHttpRequest.upload`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safelisted Request Headers"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Short List",
          "items": [
            "`Accept`, `Accept-Language`",
            "`Content-Language`",
            "`Content-Type` (safelisted values only)",
            "`Range` (simple range values)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`X-API-Key`, `Authorization`, `X-Requested-With`: not safelisted",
            "Even a safelisted header can exceed byte limits",
            "Over-long values silently force a preflight"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Concrete Calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// simple: no OPTIONS at all",
            "fetch(u, {method:'POST',",
            "  body: new URLSearchParams({a:1})})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hidden Triggers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Upload progress listener on `xhr.upload`",
            "`ReadableStream` passed as the body",
            "Safelisted header value over the byte limit",
            "Any header you forgot a library adds"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const x = new XMLHttpRequest()",
            "x.upload.onprogress = show",
            "x.open('POST', u); x.send(fd)",
            "// listener => OPTIONS first"
          ],
          "note": "no upload listener, no preflight"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Why the Safelist Exists: Does It Preflight?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why This Set Exists"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Simple = shapes an HTML `<form>` could already send",
            "Those shapes were reachable before CORS existed",
            "So no permission probe can be required for them",
            "The safelist is a compatibility fossil, not a design"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Does It Preflight?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Request",
            "Preflight?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`GET`, no extra headers",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`POST` form-urlencoded",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`POST` `application/json`",
              "**yes**"
            ],
            [
              "`DELETE` anything",
              "**yes**"
            ],
            [
              "`GET` + `X-API-Key`",
              "**yes**"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Stay Simple On Purpose",
          "text": "A plain `GET` with no custom headers never preflights — the ==cheapest== cross-origin call you can make."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Simple-Request CSRF & The OPTIONS Probe",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "CSRF Is Still Yours",
          "text": "A simple cross-origin POST reaches your handler and runs before any CORS check happens. CORS never stopped the write."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Can I dodge preflight on a JSON API?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Yes: send `Content-Type: text/plain`, parse manually",
            "Server does `JSON.parse(rawBody)` itself",
            "But you delete the browser's CSRF-ish speed bump",
            "Only do it with real anti-CSRF tokens in place"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "fetch(u,{method:'POST',",
            "  headers:{'Content-Type':'text/plain'},",
            "  body: JSON.stringify(payload)})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Preflight Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An automatic `OPTIONS` request the browser sends before the real one, asking permission for the method and headers."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "OPTIONS probe",
              "server 204",
              "cached?",
              "real PUT",
              "second CORS check"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Probe Sends"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "OPTIONS /v1/items HTTP/1.1",
            "Origin: https://app.com",
            "Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT",
            "Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,x-api-key"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Requested headers arrive lowercased, comma-separated",
            "Preflight carries no body",
            "It must be answerable without auth"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Server Must Answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Header",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Allow-Origin`",
              "who may read"
            ],
            [
              "`Allow-Methods`",
              "`GET, POST, PUT, DELETE`"
            ],
            [
              "`Allow-Headers`",
              "every non-safelisted header"
            ],
            [
              "status",
              "200 or 204, no body"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Allow-Methods` answers the preflight, not per-route policy",
            "`Allow-Headers: *` works only without credentials",
            "Every custom header must be named, or the probe fails"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Preflight Failures & Credential Modes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Classic Breakages"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Auth middleware runs first, returns `401` to OPTIONS",
            "Router has no OPTIONS handler: `404` or `405`",
            "Redirects are never followed on preflight",
            "A `http`→`https` `301` on OPTIONS kills the exchange"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "401 Reads As CORS",
          "text": "The browser reports a CORS error, never an auth error, when OPTIONS returns 401. Look at the OPTIONS status line first, always."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading It In DevTools"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Filter the network tab by method OPTIONS",
            "Diff `Access-Control-Request-Headers` against `Allow-Headers`",
            "Compare line by line — one missing name fails all",
            "Preflight fail = real request never sent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Server Log Tell",
          "items": [
            "Only an `OPTIONS` line appears",
            "No matching `PUT`/`POST` line",
            "That means the probe was rejected",
            "Not a client bug — a config bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Two Checks, Not One",
          "text": "The real response must also carry a valid ACAO. Preflight approval alone grants nothing; the second check can still fail."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Preflight costs a full round trip. On a high-latency link it can roughly double perceived API latency."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Credentials Are Opt-In",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Cookies sent?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`same-origin` (default)",
              "only same-origin"
            ],
            [
              "`include`",
              "yes, cross-origin"
            ],
            [
              "`omit`",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "`xhr.withCredentials = true`",
              "XHR equivalent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`include` also sends TLS client certs",
            "`include` lets `Set-Cookie` in the response stick",
            "Default mode sends nothing cross-origin"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Wildcard Ban",
          "text": "With credentials, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is rejected outright. The server must echo the exact origin string back."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Credentials: Client & Server Opt-In",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Both Gates Must Open"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Client side",
                "lines": [
                  "`credentials:'include'`",
                  "or `withCredentials`",
                  "one alone = no cookie"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Server side",
                "lines": [
                  "`Allow-Credentials: true`",
                  "exact origin echo",
                  "`Vary: Origin`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Client Opt-In"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "fetch(u, {credentials:'include'})",
            "// XHR equivalent:",
            "const x = new XMLHttpRequest()",
            "x.withCredentials = true"
          ],
          "note": "default mode sends no cookies"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Server Opt-In"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Access-Control-Allow-Origin:",
            "  https://app.com",
            "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true",
            "Vary: Origin"
          ],
          "note": "never `*` here"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "One Side Only",
          "items": [
            "Client `include`, no server header: read ==blocked==",
            "Server `true`, client default: no cookie sent",
            "Both set: cookies flow, JS reads",
            "Preflight needs `Allow-Credentials` too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Silent Failure",
          "text": "If the client forgets `include`, no console error appears — the cookie simply never leaves. Check the request's `Cookie` header first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Wildcard Ban, Vary: Origin & SameSite",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same ban hits `Allow-Headers: *` and `Allow-Methods: *`",
            "And `Expose-Headers: *` — literal `*`, not a wildcard",
            "Preflight must ALSO return `Allow-Credentials: true`",
            "Missing that header blocks the read even if ACAO is right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Exact Error"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "The value of the Access-Control-Allow-Origin",
            "header must not be the wildcard '*' when the",
            "request's credentials mode is 'include'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cache Safety With Echo"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Echoing an origin makes the response origin-dependent",
            "Without `Vary: Origin` a shared cache mixes them up",
            "One tenant then receives another tenant's ACAO",
            "So `Vary: Origin` is mandatory, not optional"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SameSite Is A Second Gate"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SameSite=Lax` is the modern default",
            "Lax blocks the cookie on cross-site fetch/XHR",
            "Even with CORS fully, correctly configured",
